 "answer": {
  "answer": "The study confirmed 2 of the 5 cases it set out to find. Two combinations, on two different scenes, make the policy collide at a rate surely above 0.5: in 096988dd, the car 1.5 s early at recorded speed with the ego at 1.2x (S4); and in 19f339ba, the car 1 s late at 1.5x speed with the ego at 1.4x (S26). Every repeat at both settings failed. Every failure was the policy's fault and none looks like a simulator artifact. In each one the ego drifted left out of its lane and its front hit a car driving alongside in the next lane. That car was not the one the study retimed, so the knobs probably make an existing weakness show up rather than set up the conflict. None of the other 8 scenes failed at any setting tried. Most of those settings ran only once or twice, so they are hints, not rates, and the goal of 5 confirmed cases was not met.",
  "findings": [
